{"lines": ["A Navy warship filmed something drop into the Pacific.", "The Pentagon confirmed the video is real.", "In July 2019, off San Diego, the USS Omaha's thermal camera locked onto a dark ball.", "It glided. It stopped. Then it sank toward the waves.", "On the tape, a sailor shouts: It splashed! It splashed!", "That's what the screen shows. Now the sea.", "The filmmaker who leaked the clip says a Navy submarine searched the spot.", "It found nothing. No wreckage. No debris.", "He also says the ball was about six feet wide, and that it had flown for about an hour.", "The Pentagon only said the video was taken by Navy personnel, and passed it to its team for unexplained sightings.", "Something went into the ocean.", "Nothing was ever pulled out.", "Nobody explained it."], "words": [["A", 0.0, 0.1], ["Navy", 0.1, 0.28], ["warship", 0.28, 0.92], ["filmed", 0.92, 1.14], ["something", 1.14, 1.64], ["drop", 1.64, 1.92], ["into", 1.92, 2.18], ["the", 2.18, 2.32], ["Pacific.", 2.32, 2.6], ["The", 3.44, 3.5], ["Pentagon", 3.5, 3.76], ["confirmed", 3.76, 4.36], ["the", 4.36, 4.68], ["video", 4.68, 4.96], ["is", 4.96, 5.28], ["real.", 5.28, 5.54], ["In", 6.06, 6.16], ["July", 6.16, 6.28], ["2019,", 6.28, 7.0], ["off", 7.5, 7.6], ["San", 7.6, 7.88], ["Diego,", 7.88, 8.24], ["the", 8.8, 8.86], ["USS", 8.86, 9.18], ["Omaha's", 9.18, 9.96], ["thermal", 9.96, 10.12], ["camera", 10.12, 10.52], ["locked", 10.52, 10.86], ["onto", 10.86, 11.16], ["a", 11.16, 11.32], ["dark", 11.32, 11.52], ["ball.", 11.52, 11.82], ["It", 12.3, 12.38], ["glided.", 12.38, 12.8], ["It", 13.36, 13.42], ["stopped.", 13.42, 13.7], ["Then", 14.42, 14.46], ["it", 14.46, 14.56], ["sank", 14.56, 14.8], ["toward", 14.8, 15.2], ["the", 15.2, 15.4], ["waves.", 15.4, 15.64], ["On", 16.32, 16.36], ["the", 16.36, 16.48], ["tape,", 16.48, 16.7], ["a", 16.7, 16.9], ["sailor", 16.9, 17.12], ["shouts:", 17.12, 17.56], ["It", 18.1, 18.24], ["splashed!", 18.24, 18.68], ["It", 19.18, 19.32], ["splashed!", 19.32, 19.66],